kussack@isit.fhg.de (Renata Kussack) writes:

>Maybe a stupid question: From which corpses can I get the intrinsics
>regeneration and teleport control from? -- Thanks for attention.

As your teachers will have told you a lot before, asking a question is
never stupid: not asking a question is...

But to get to the answer: TP control you can get from a tengu or the
Wizard of Yendor. Don't eat the latter one if you are human though:
cannibalism is considered inappropriate.

You cannot get regeneration from a corpse. You CAN get them as an
intrinsic though: polymorph yourself into a monster that can eat
certain rings, and eat the appropriate ring. There is a 1/3 chance that
you will get the intrinsic. The same goes for some other rings as well,
like rings of gain stat.

Note that you cannot eat all rings, and the ring of regeneration is a
different one every game. Also, having regeneration as an intrinsic
means you consume your food much faster than usual (like when you are
wearing the ring).

More specific information can be ftp-ed from ftp.krl.caltech.edu, in
/pub/nethack/rings.eat

